      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norwich%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office has served Norwich since 1828, keeping the village connected for nearly two centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norwich%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Norwich was incorporated as a village in 1833, just six years after its first post office opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norwich%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The National Road and Zane Grey Museum in Norwich preserves the history of the National Road and honors the western novelist Zane Grey.",
